july-ibus (0.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Renamed the project from "Bornona IBus" to "July" (the Bornona
    layout itself keeps its name — July is the product, Bornona is the
    keyboard layout it ships). Replaces/Conflicts/Provides
    bornona-ibus so upgrading from the old package works cleanly.
  * Fix h/r sitting invisibly as a pending key with no way to appear
    until an unrelated later keystroke happened to resolve or flush
    it -- and being silently lost entirely on focus-out before this,
    not just delayed. Added a 400ms auto-flush timeout, and
    focus-out/reset now flush the pending glyph instead of discarding
    it.
  * New in-bar user guide ("?" button): the full Bornona key mapping,
    with a বাংলা/English toggle, glyphs computed live so it can't
    drift out of sync with actual typing behavior.
  * Fix floating bar silently crashing on startup on desktops without
    AppIndicator3/AyatanaAppIndicator3 (e.g. plain Ubuntu GNOME) --
    the bar now degrades gracefully with minimize-to-tray disabled
    instead of failing to launch at all.
  * Harden IBus engine auto-selection against a GLib.Error some setups
    raise when no global engine has ever been configured.
  * Bar window now always shows first; IBus setup happens afterward
    and can no longer prevent the window from appearing.
  * Uncaught startup errors now print a real traceback to stderr
    instead of failing silently with no diagnostic trail.

 -- July project <imdashraful17@gmail.com>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 05:15:00 +0600

